# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The App's website: environment variables.
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill values in as you complete each gate
# (M1 to M11 in SETUP.md / plan.md). `.env.local` is git-ignored; never commit
# real values. In production, set the same values in Vercel:
# Project Settings -> Environment Variables. Mark secrets as "Sensitive".
#
# The site boots with any of these blank. A feature that needs a missing value
# fails with an error naming the gate to complete. Each step adds its own
# variables here when it needs them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- M1: The App's database ---
# DATABASE_URL is the POOLED connection string (host contains "-pooler"); the site
# uses it at runtime. DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED is the DIRECT string; migrations
# (npm run db:migrate) use it (POSTGRES_URL_NON_POOLING, its older name, works too).
# Both come from Vercel -> Storage -> lawn-care-app-db -> .env.local tab (Show secret);
# pasting that block as it is works.
DATABASE_URL=
DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED=
